{"v":[[1,"Paul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ, and Timothy our brother, unto Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellowlabourer,"],[2,"And to our beloved Apphia, and Archippus our fellowsoldier, and to the church in thy house:"],[3,"Grace to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."],[4,"I thank my God, making mention of thee always in my prayers,"],[5,"Hearing of thy love and faith, which thou hast toward the Lord Jesus, and toward all saints;"],[6,"That the communication of thy faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in Christ Jesus."],[7,"For we have great joy and consolation in thy love, because the bowels of the saints are refreshed by thee, brother."],[8,"Wherefore, though I might be much bold in Christ to enjoin thee that which is convenient,"],[9,"Yet for love’s sake I rather beseech thee, being such an one as Paul the aged, and now also a prisoner of Jesus Christ."],[10,"I beseech thee for my son Onesimus, whom I have begotten in my bonds:"],[11,"Which in time past was to thee unprofitable, but now profitable to thee and to me:"],[12,"Whom I have sent again: thou therefore receive him, that is, mine own bowels:"],[13,"Whom I would have retained with me, that in thy stead he might have ministered unto me in the bonds of the gospel:"],[14,"But without thy mind would I do nothing; that thy benefit should not be as it were of necessity, but willingly."],[15,"For perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that thou shouldest receive him for ever;"],[16,"Not now as a servant, but above a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more unto thee, both in the flesh, and in the Lord?"],[17,"If thou count me therefore a partner, receive him as myself."],[18,"If he hath wronged thee, or oweth thee ought, put that on mine account;"],[19,"I Paul have written it with mine own hand, I will repay it: albeit I do not say to thee how thou owest unto me even thine own self besides."],[20,"Yea, brother, let me have joy of thee in the Lord: refresh my bowels in the Lord."],[21,"Having confidence in thy obedience I wrote unto thee, knowing that thou wilt also do more than I say."],[22,"But withal prepare me also a lodging: for I trust that through your prayers I shall be given unto you."],[23,"There salute thee Epaphras, my fellowprisoner in Christ Jesus;"],[24,"Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, Lucas, my fellowlabourers."],[25,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.  Written from Rome to Philemon, by Onesimus a servant."]],"w":{"1":[["Paulos","Paul","G3972"],["desmios","a prisoner","G1198"],["Christou","of Christ","G5547"],["Iēsou","Jesus","G2424"],["kai","and","G2532"],["Timotheos","Timothy","G5095"],["ho","<the>","G3588"],["adelphos","[our] brother","G80"],["Philēmoni","To Philemon","G5371"],["tō","the","G3588"],["agapētō","beloved","G27"],["kai","and","G2532"],["sunergō","fellow worker","G4904"],["hēmōn","of us","G3165"]],"2":[["kai","and","G2532"],["Apphia","to Apphia","G682"],["tē","<the>","G3588"],["kai","and","G2532"],["Archippō","to Archippus","G751"],["tō","the","G3588"],["sustratiōtē","fellow soldier","G4961"],["hēmōn","of us","G3165"],["kai","and","G2532"],["tē","to the","G3588"],["kat᾽","at","G2596"],["oikon","[the] house","G3624"],["sou","of you","G4771"],["ekklēsia","church:","G1577"]],"3":[["charis","Grace","G5485"],["humin","to you","G4771"],["kai","and","G2532"],["eirēnē","peace","G1515"],["apo","from","G575"],["theou","God","G2316"],["patros","Father","G3962"],["hēmōn","of us","G3165"],["kai","and","G2532"],["kuriou","[the] Lord","G2962"],["Iēsou","Jesus","G2424"],["Christou","Christ.","G5547"]],"4":[["Eucharistō","I thank","G2168"],["tō","the","G3588"],["theō","God","G2316"],["mou","of mine","G3165"],["pantote","always","G3842"],["mneian","mention","G3417"],["sou","of you","G4771"],["poioumenos","making","G4160"],["epi","upon","G1909"],["tōn","the","G3588"],["proseuchōn","prayers","G4335"],["mou","of mine,","G3165"]],"5":[["akou